>>__ Parse.temp_set_grammars $ valOf $ grammarDB {thyname="hol"};
## `register_frac_type_rat`

``` hol4
Refute.register_frac_type_rat : unit -> unit
```

------------------------------------------------------------------------

Restores or refreshes Refute's built-in rational fraction registration.

The built-in registration maps the nullary `rat` type and its arithmetic,
comparison, numeral, and constructor constants to the corresponding
normalized `refute` fraction operations.  It also installs the display
postprocessor that reconstructs model values with `rat_cons`.

The operation validates all fraction metadata before changing state and
commits the fraction and display registrations together.  It is
session-local, synchronized, atomic, and idempotent.  The registration is
installed when `Refute` is loaded; this entry point is useful after
session-level customization of the `rat` fraction or postprocessor rows.
It creates no HOL objects.

### Failure

Fails if the required `rat` or `refute` constants are unavailable or if
`rat` has an incompatible datatype or codatatype classification.  A
failure leaves both registries unchanged.

### See also

[`Refute.register_frac_type`](#Refute.register_frac_type),
[`Refute.register_ersatz`](#Refute.register_ersatz),
[`Refute.register_term_postprocessor`](#Refute.register_term_postprocessor),
[`Refute.model_refute`](#Refute.model_refute)

Rational model display is described in \ref{Description:the-holrefute-library}.
